{"assets":["/statement-assets/2cbae166f6bfad869ed7e3febdcdfd97325fe2d4d007a0da538b3b7f4f32f35c.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1486","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Pairs of Paths"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"6 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a tree consisting of $$$n$$$ vertices, and $$$m$$$ simple vertex paths. Your task is to find how many pairs of those paths intersect at exactly one vertex. More formally you have to find the number of pairs $$$(i, j)$$$ $$$(1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq m)$$$ such that $$$path_i$$$ and $$$path_j$$$ have exactly one vertex in common. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ $$$(1 \\leq n \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^5)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next $$$n - 1$$$ lines describe the tree. Each line contains two integers $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$ $$$(1 \\leq u, v \\leq n)$$$ describing an edge between vertices $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next line contains a single integer $$$m$$$ $$$(1 \\leq m \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^5)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next $$$m$$$ lines describe paths. Each line describes a path by it's two endpoints $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$ $$$(1 \\leq u, v \\leq n)$$$. The given path is all the vertices on the shortest path from $$$u$$$ to $$$v$$$ (including $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer — the number of pairs of paths that intersect at exactly one vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n1 2\n1 3\n1 4\n3 5\n4\n2 3\n2 4\n3 4\n3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n3\n1 1\n1 1\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n1 2\n1 3\n1 4\n3 5\n6\n2 3\n2 4\n3 4\n3 5\n1 1\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/2cbae166f6bfad869ed7e3febdcdfd97325fe2d4d007a0da538b3b7f4f32f35c.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The tree in the first example and paths look like this. Pairs $$$(1,4)$$$ and $$$(3,4)$$$ intersect at one vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example all three paths contain the same single vertex, so all pairs $$$(1, 2)$$$, $$$(1, 3)$$$ and $$$(2, 3)$$$ intersect at one vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third example is the same as the first example with two additional paths. Pairs $$$(1,4)$$$, $$$(1,5)$$$, $$$(2,5)$$$, $$$(3,4)$$$, $$$(3,5)$$$, $$$(3,6)$$$ and $$$(5,6)$$$ intersect at one vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1486F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1486/problem/F"}